  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-11-13 from the official Southern Utah University 2026-2027 General Catalog (current edition, catoid=28) Social Work (BSW) program page and its linked official degree map, 'Social Work Degree Maps (2026-2027)', tab 'Social Work (Campus)', last updated/reviewed August 3, 2026 (the workbook Index lists Online as N/A for this program). Semester placement is the university's official sample 4-year campus academic plan (SUU Program Maps, 2026-2027), which the source itself labels a guide only; students confirm specifics in Degree Works with a Student Success Advisor. The catalog prints 'Total Credits, BSW Degree: 120', which the map matches exactly (15/16/16/15/15/15/15/13). The map exercises the full catalog Social Work Curriculum of 58 credits: Social Work 39 (SW 1010, SW 2100, SW 3100, SW 3200, SW 3300, SW 3350, SW 3370, SW 3600, SW 4500, SW 4891 at 6 credits, SW 4892 at 6 credits), Family Life & Human Development 12 (FLHD 1500/4100/4250/4350), and Social Work Support 7 (MATH 1040 at 4 credits, NFS 1020). Catalog titles are recorded where the map abbreviates (NFS 1020). The map carries a Spring Year 2 banner, 'Apply to Bachelor of Social Work Program'. Per the catalog, students must earn a C (2.0) or better in all Social Work curriculum courses, admission to the BSW program requires completion of SW 1010, SW 2100 and NFS 1020 with a cumulative GPA of 2.5 or higher, and students complete 450 hours of field practicum in the senior year; the program is accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE).",
